=pod

=head1 NAME

changetrack-ng - system file change tracker

=head1 SYNOPSIS

  changetrack-ng [options] [subcommand] [args]

=head1 DESCRIPTION

B<changetrack-ng> tracks changes to system files and directories using a
pluggable VCS backend (RCS, Git, Fossil, SVN, or Mercurial) and notifies
via one or more channels (email, webhook, OTLP, file log).

On each run it compares file metadata and content against the last recorded
state, commits any changes to the VCS repository, and dispatches notifications.
It is designed to run hourly from cron or a systemd timer.

=head1 SUBCOMMANDS

=over 4

=item B<run> (default)

Scan all tracked files, commit detected changes, and send notifications.
This is the default subcommand when none is specified.

=item B<init>

Explicitly initialize the VCS output repository.  Under normal operation
this happens automatically on the first run; use this to pre-initialize
without scanning.

=item B<status>

List files that have changed since the last commit.  Exits 0 if nothing
has changed, 1 if changes were found.

=item B<diff> [I<path>]

Show a unified diff of pending changes.  If I<path> is given, show the
diff for that file only; otherwise show all pending diffs.

=item B<log> [I<path>]

Show VCS history.  If I<path> is given, show history for that file only.

=item B<revert> I<path> I<rev>

Restore I<path> to revision I<rev> in the VCS.  Prompts for confirmation
unless B<--force> is given.

=item B<update-ignore>

Write or refresh the VCS-native ignore file (e.g., C<.gitignore>) using the
built-in defaults plus any patterns in the config C<ignore> key.

=item B<migrate-config> I<v1-config> [I<v2-output>]

Read a legacy C<changetrack> v1 config file and write an equivalent v2 INI
file.  If I<v2-output> is omitted it is derived from I<v1-config> with
C<.ng.conf> suffix.

=back

=head1 OPTIONS

=over 4

=item B<-c>, B<--config> I<file>

Config file path.  Default: C</etc/changetrack-ng/changetrack-ng.conf>.

=item B<-m>, B<--message> I<msg>

Annotation string appended to the VCS commit message.  Used by package
manager hooks to identify the triggering operation, e.g.,
C<-m 'post-install: apt'>.

=item B<--no-auto-init>

Disable automatic VCS initialization on first run.  The command will abort
if the repository is not already initialized.

=item B<-n>, B<--dry-run>

Detect and report pending changes without mutating VCS state, writing
metadata, or sending notifications.

=item B<-f>, B<--force>

Bypass interactive confirmation prompts (e.g., for B<revert>).

=item B<-q>, B<--quiet>

Suppress all progress output.  Warnings and errors are still written to
stderr.

=item B<-v>, B<--verbose>

Enable verbose debug output showing per-step internal state.

=item B<-V>, B<--version>

Print version number and exit.

=item B<-h>, B<--help>

Print a usage summary and exit.

=back

=head1 EXIT STATUS

=over 4

=item B<0>

Success, or lock held (silent skip).

=item B<1>

Status subcommand: files changed.  Revert: aborted by user.

=item B<2>

Runtime error (VCS failure, unhandled exception).

=item B<64>

Usage error (bad arguments, config parse failure, unknown subcommand).

=item B<75>

Lock timeout exceeded.

=back

=head1 FILES

=over 4

=item F</etc/changetrack-ng/changetrack-ng.conf>

Default configuration file.  See L<changetrack-ng.conf(5)>.

=item F</var/lib/changetrack-ng/>

Default VCS output directory.

=item F</var/run/changetrack-ng.lock>

Default lock file.

=item F</etc/cron.hourly/changetrack-ng>

Installed by C<make install-cron>.  No-ops when the systemd timer is active.

=item F</etc/systemd/system/changetrack-ng.timer>

Installed by C<make install-systemd>.

=back

=head1 EXAMPLES

Track changes hourly via cron:

  sudo make install install-cron

Initialize the repository explicitly and do a first scan:

  sudo changetrack-ng init
  sudo changetrack-ng run

Check what has changed since the last run:

  sudo changetrack-ng status

View the diff for a specific file:

  sudo changetrack-ng diff /etc/passwd

Revert a file to a specific Git commit:

  sudo changetrack-ng revert /etc/passwd abc1234

Migrate a legacy changetrack config:

  sudo changetrack-ng migrate-config /etc/changetrack.conf

